<<<
ee Ay, ay, sir is usually written thus; the commoner now for ever; on the other hand the ayes have it is usual, though there be intended for the

spellin

is probably

-es may

plural termination.

the other side.
===
+ *Ay, ay, sir* is usually written thus; & *aye* is probably the commoner spelling now for *ever*; on the other hand *the ayes have it* is usual, though *-es* may there be intended for the plural termination. *Ay* (I) yes, *aye* (ā) ever, seems likely to prevail; but the authority of the OED is on the other side.
>>>

